fix.summary_for_maintainer:
What pilot 4 trains: a 2,000,000-step fine-tune of each pilot-3 walker's own 8M checkpoint (seeds 42, 52, 60) on the same T. rex locomotion stage, with R6 unchanged. On top of R6:
- a live "go straight" command on the reserved inputs (heading mode, 1.5 m/s, no turns, no stops);
- the prey moved onto the spawn line;
- a heading price of -0.2 x min(|error| / 0.5 rad, 1) per step.
Entry shaping is off: no warm-up, a constant forward weight of 2.0, and each walker keeps its own log_std. Proposed cadence: an evaluation every 65,536 steps and a checkpoint every 250,000 [measured: TOML].

Code: local branch claude/pilot-walk-r10-p4 at 7700f28, 11 pilot-only commits on 31d02e42, nothing pushed [measured].
- Seven come from the build: the TOML command table becomes the dataclass; the task digest derives the command section; this one stage may load its own checkpoint; the 11 behaviour recipes do not inherit the new keys; the default-off price; the pilot-4 TOML.
- Four are new review fixes:
  - the self-load admits only a command-free checkpoint, so a pilot-4 checkpoint can only be resumed;
  - the command table's numbers must be real numbers, and the "heading" rule is applied where the task is hashed;
  - the price keys must be numbers, with a new test at other weights and scales;
  - a test that a recipe's own [env] wins, plus two corrected TOML comments.
- Digest: only 8 T. rex locomotion lines moved, all at commit 7; the fixes move none [measured].
- Tests: 2705 passed and 4 failed (the 4 known tests that pin main's recipe digests; they fail at 31d02e42 too), with 0 training-guard hits. ruff and mypy are clean [measured].
- The new tests fail on the unfixed code and catch the review's three surviving mutants [measured].

At the start the walkers act exactly as in pilot 3 (equal actions, command inputs zeroed). They still curve, every episode the same way: -23 / -26 / -43 deg on reset 3042. The price costs them about 28-98 per episode, 1-3% of return, and all three straightness parts fail at entry [measured as recorded: setup check and draft].

Straightness is judged at 2M, only on seeds that still WALK by pilot 3's rule. Proposed bars:
- (a) end-heading change: |median| <= 5 deg and p95 <= 15 deg;
- (b) the 1-s mean heading stays within 11.5 deg of the command (p95), and the instantaneous heading within 18.5 deg (p95, a guard against zig-zags);
- (c) after a +-15 deg nudge at 6.5 s, counted only once the prey is passed, the 1-s mean error at 9.5 s has median <= 5 deg and p95 <= 11.5 deg. It is NOT READ if fewer than 30 episodes count;
- plus a straightness look at a top-down plot.
Each seed is STRAIGHT WALKS, STRAIGHT NO RECOVERY, CURVED WALKS or NOT WALKS; the pilot outcome is the label at least 2 of the 3 seeds share.

Cost: about 2 L4-hours per seed, about 6 L4-hours in all; allow 3 h per runtime [inferred from pilot 3's speed].

Decisions, recommended option first (26 in all; the full list is in the text):
- the bars above (1, 20), with D as the weave measure (2);
- the 6.5-s nudge, counted after the prey pass (3, 19, 25);
- parents read from Drive by path, with the judge binding each sha256 (4); the notebook's manual cell (5); s42 stays (6);
- cadence 65,536 / 250,000, judged at 0.5 / 1 / 1.5 / 2M (7); judge in the pilot-4 env only (8);
- a look with veto power, for every seed passing (a) and (b) (10, 21);
- resume from any checkpoint pair at or after 250k (11); collapse reference 1064.0 (12); keep the command table and production's [ppo] schedules (13, 17);
- hold the launch unless every prepared parent WALKS in the pilot-4 env (24); no diagnostics change (26);
- then approve the commits and the text, OK the push and the launch (18).
